      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T15:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this makes sense, but I believe we should encourage disclosing AI-assisted contributions.\n\nI often use the AI capabilities in IntelliJ; should I then add `Assisted-By: IntelliJ`?\n\nWhat is the added value for the reviewer? Is it a warning sign of low quality? Should we also include the model?\n\n\u003e Other Google projects do that [1].\n\nIf this is a Google-specific requirement, I don\u0027t have any objections. @hariprak@google.com can you check internally at Google?\n\n\u003e If we don\u0027t want to explicitly mention the tool, we can just add a generic git trailer `Assisted-By: AI` or any other way of making it clear.\n\nI have no objection to a generic `Assisted-By: AI`, but I do not understand its value.\n\n\u003e We could ask to add it only if the AI-generated content was \"substantial\".\n\nWhat do you mean by _\"substantial\"_? 10%? 20%? 50%?\nIf the generation means _\"I don\u0027t have a clue because it was generated\"_ I fear that allowing us to simply tag the change as `Assisted-By: AI` could be used as a scapegoat for not taking responsibility.\n\nHowever, if Google has this requirement in the commit message, I would not object to it.\n\u003e \n\u003e [1]: https://github.com/google/gvisor/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#label-ai-assisted-work",
      "parentUuid": "ae925632_a0c3d222",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "d936dee47d0f001cea35abca1c9e5ba78a76d543",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
